This includes:
1. Talking with your doctor or therapist about how you're feeling;
2. Calling a crisis hotline, such as the National Suicide Prevention Lifeline at 1-800-273-TALK (8255) in the United States; 
3. Reaching out to friends, family members, or trusted individuals who can offer support and guidance;
4. Contacting local mental health resources or emergency services in your area. 

Please do prioritize your own life and seek immediate assistance from qualified professionals if you feel overwhelmed or think you might hurt yourself. There are people ready to listen and help!
